.TH RELEASE-NOTE 1 "October 2026" "release-note 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
release-note \- turn a release's GitHub/GitLab issues into a polished, persona\-grouped release note
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B release-note
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B release-note
selects the issues of one release, drafts a user\-facing release note with the GLM Coding Plan
API (an OpenAI\-compatible endpoint), and writes it as markdown. It ships three surfaces: a local
web UI (
.BR "release-note serve" ),
a scriptable CLI, and CI recipes for GitHub Actions and GitLab CI.
.PP
Issue selection works by explicit refs (#123, URLs, files), by exact label, by release PR
expansion (a release PR's referenced issues are pulled in automatically), or by
release\-label discovery: issues tagged e.g.
.I "Release v1.19"
are grouped by the version inside the label and the newest group becomes the current release \-
with the version picked up automatically.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B generate
Fetch a release's issues and generate the note. See OPTIONS and EXAMPLES.
.TP
.B serve
Start the local web UI (default
.IR http://127.0.0.1:4310 ).
.B --port
.I n
overrides the port. The server binds 127.0.0.1 only and has no auth \- never expose it.
.TP
.B config
Show or edit the stored settings:
.BR list " (default), " get " " <field> ", " set " " <field> " " <value> ", " path .
Fields:
.BR glmApiKey ", " glmBaseUrl ", " glmModel ", " defaultRepo ", " productName ", " outputDir .
.TP
.B check
Verify provider authentication and repository access.
.B --repo
.IR owner/name ,
.B --provider
.IR name .
.TP
.B test-key
Verify the GLM API key with an 8\-token request.
.B --api-key ,
.B --base-url ,
.B --model
override the stored settings.
.TP
.B man
Show this manual page (also available as
.B man release-note
after a global npm install).
.TP
.BR help " [" command ]
Show help. The global \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR flags also work.
.SH GENERATE OPTIONS
.SS Issue selection
.TP
.BI --issue " ref"
Issue ref: #123, 123, or a full GitHub/GitLab URL. Repeatable; also accepted as bare
positional arguments. \fB@file\fR reads one ref per line from a file, \fB\-\fR reads stdin.
.TP
.BI --release-pr " n"
Expand a release PR: every issue referenced in its body and comments is fetched too.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --label " label"
Select every issue/PR carrying this exact label. Repeatable; the union is fetched.
.TP
.BI --release-label-prefix " [prefix]"
Auto\-discover the current release: issues whose labels start with the prefix (default
.IR "Release v" )
are grouped by the version in the label and the newest group is selected.
.SS Version
The first of these wins: \fB--version\fR; the highest release label on the selected issues;
\fB--bump\fR from a base version.
.TP
.BI --version " v"
Exact version, e.g. 1.19.
.TP
.BI --bump " patch|minor|major"
Bump a base version: \fB--from\fR \fIv\fR, or the newest \fIrelease\-note\-v*.md\fR in the
output folder. major: 1.18 -> 2.0; minor: 1.18 -> 1.19; patch: 1.18 -> 1.18.1.
.TP
.BI --from " v"
Base version for \fB--bump\fR.
.SS Hotfixes and content
.TP
.BI --hotfix " n,n,…"
Mark these issue numbers as hotfixes (the 🔥 Hotfixes section).
.TP
.BI --hotfix-label " label"
Mark every selected issue carrying this label as a hotfix.
.TP
.BI --repo " owner/name"
Target repository. Default: \fB--repo\fR, the
.I defaultRepo
setting, then the CI repo (\fICI_PROJECT_PATH\fR / \fIGITHUB_REPOSITORY\fR).
.TP
.BI --date " YYYY-MM-DD"
Release date (default: today).
.TP
.BI --instructions " text" | --instructions-file " path"
Extra instructions for the model (mutually exclusive).
.TP
.BI --context-file " path"
Attach a local file as context. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --product " name"
Product name for the note header (default: the \fIproductName\fR setting).
.SS Output and connection
.TP
.BI --out " path|"
Write the note to a file; \fB\-\fR (default) writes stdout. Existing files are refused unless
\fB--force\fR is given.
.TP
.BI --provider " name"
.BR gh-cli " (default locally), " github-api ", or " gitlab-api .
.TP
.BI --api-key " key" | --base-url " url" | --model " id"
Per\-run GLM overrides.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress progress output on stderr.
.SH PROVIDERS
The web UI always uses the
.B gh CLI
(whatever account
.B gh auth login
knows). Headless runs pick a token\-based REST provider automatically:
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
github-api|GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN|GitHub Actions (GITHUB_ACTIONS=true)
gitlab-api|GITLAB_TOKEN|GitLab CI (GITLAB_CI=true)
gh-cli|gh auth login|local terminals
.TE
.PP
Set \fBRELEASE_NOTE_PROVIDER\fR or \fB--provider\fR to override. In GitHub Actions grant
\fBpermissions: issues: read\fR; on GitLab use a project access token with
\fBread_api\fR (\fBCI_JOB_TOKEN\fR cannot read the issues API).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_GLM_API_KEY
GLM API key (overrides config.local.json).
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_GLM_BASE_URL
API endpoint (default: https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4).
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_GLM_MODEL
Model (default: glm\-5.3\-flash).
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_DEFAULT_REPO
Default repository.
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_PRODUCT_NAME
Product name used in the note header.
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_OUTPUT_DIR
Where notes are saved (default: \fIreleases/\fR inside the tool folder).
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_PROVIDER
Force a backend: gh\-cli, github\-api, or gitlab\-api.
.TP
.B RELEASE_NOTE_PORT
Web UI port (default 4310).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I config.local.json
Stored settings; git\-ignored, never committed.
.TP
.I samples/format-example.md
The output contract \- structure, headings, and tone of the generated note. Replace it with
your own format.
.TP
.I data/releases/
Web\-UI release store (one JSON per release); user data, git\-ignored.
.TP
.I releases/
Default output folder for saved notes.
.TP
.I examples/
Ready\-to\-copy GitHub Actions workflow and GitLab CI job.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on runtime failure (including partially failed issue fetches \- the note may
still have been written); 2 on usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
Generate the current release (version comes from its \fIRelease v1.19\fR\-style labels):
.PP
.nf
.RS
release-note generate \-\-repo owner/repo \-\-release\-label\-prefix
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inside GitHub Actions with the repository's own token:
.PP
.nf
.RS
release\-note generate \-\-provider github\-api \-\-release\-label\-prefix \-\-out note.md
.RE
.fi
.PP
Inside GitLab CI (repo from \fICI_PROJECT_PATH\fR):
.PP
.nf
.RS
release\-note generate \-\-provider gitlab\-api \-\-label "Release v1.19" \-\-out note.md
.RE
.fi
.PP
Explicit issues with a hotfix, version bumped from the last saved note:
.PP
.nf
.RS
release\-note generate \-\-repo owner/repo \-\-issue "#101 #102" \-\-release\-pr 312 \\
    \-\-hotfix 101 \-\-bump minor \-\-out releases/release\-note\-v1.20.md
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
gh(1), the project README.md, examples/ in the repository.
